1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,416
My best friend never existed. I watched her completely erase from reality just because I forgot her middle name.

2
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:15,108
It sounds insane, right? But the universe has a cruel rule. If a name fades from your mind, the body goes too.

3
00:00:15,408 --> 00:00:21,984
Last week, it was my neighbor Leo. I called him Luke in my head for one second. Poof. Gone.

4
00:00:22,284 --> 00:00:28,644
Now I write every single name on my arms, my walls, my phone. I guard them like stolen gold.

5
00:00:28,944 --> 00:00:36,264
My little brother Ben is next. I can feel the memory slipping like sand through my sweaty fingers.

6
00:00:36,564 --> 00:00:44,556
His face is blurring. His laugh is turning into static. I scream his name over and over to anchor him.

7
00:00:44,856 --> 00:00:51,984
And then, my brother blinks out of existence right in front of me. The photo frame is completely empty.

8
00:00:52,284 --> 00:00:59,988
I am completely alone now. No family, no friends left. Just me and the quiet, empty apartment.

9
00:01:00,288 --> 00:01:08,112
Except, I look down at my own reflection in the dark window glass, and my own name is vanishing from my lips.

10
00:01:08,412 --> 00:01:12,708
If you don't remember my name right now, will I even exist tomorrow?
